1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Orichalcos. A promise-kept market for AI trading agents.
Built on 0G mainnet for the Agentic Trading Arena track.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Every AI trader sits on one of two horns.
Reveal the strategy, alpha decays.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Hide it, no challenger can trust it.
No primitive for verifiable performance without revealed alpha — until now.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Three roles. A trader posts a USDC bond against a drawdown promise —
verbatim, free text, sealed inside 0G Compute TEE.

5
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:40,000
A challenger places a stake against the promise.
An LP underwrites the float. Three primitives, one verifiable trail.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Bond, sealed promise in TEE, real Hyperliquid testnet fills,
challenger stakes, breach or kept-promise, permissionless settlement.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:56,000
On breach, the bond pays the challenger.
On a kept promise, the stake splits sixty-forty.

8
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Trader earns yield for being right, LP earns the rest.
Now let me show you live on chain.

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:10,000
This is the live market on 0G mainnet, chain ID sixteen-six-sixty-one.
Every card is a wager — a trader who's posted a bond against a drawdown promise.

10
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:20,000
The headline reads the promise verbatim.
The protocol is permissionless: anyone mints, anyone stakes, anyone settles.

11
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:30,000
A trader writes their own promise. Free text.
When they hit mint, we encrypt the promise to 0G Storage,

12
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:38,000
run a real TEE inference inside Intel TDX on 0G Compute,
verify the chatId via processResponse,

13
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:42,000
and commit the result to an INFT on 0G Chain.
Four 0G components, end-to-end.

14
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:50,000
And here it is on 0G mainnet — StrategyINFT contract, chainId sixteen-six-sixty-one.
Every wager carries real TEE-verified chatIds and 0G Storage merkle roots.

15
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Now the challenger side. Pick a claim size — five hundred USDC.
Stake is twelve and a half percent up front.

16
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Two outcomes pre-computed: if the trader breaks the promise, you claim from the bond,
net plus four hundred thirty-seven.

17
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,000
If they keep it, your stake pays the trader for being right.

18
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:22,000
And this is the trust layer. Every trade carries a TEE attestation chatId —
sealed inference on 0G Compute.

19
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,000
A 0G Storage merkle root for the reasoning bundle.
And the actual Hyperliquid testnet transaction hash.

20
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:35,000
And here's the proof. A wager that kept its promise.
The settlement transaction emits PolicyExpired —

21
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:43,000
premium to LP, two point five USDC;
premium to trader, three point seven five USDC.

22
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:50,000
That's the sixty-forty split, settled on chain by any wallet calling settleEpoch.
Bond, stake, settlement — all verifiable.

23
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Orichalcos. Built for Track Two on 0G mainnet.
